import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DelaunayStretch_SigmaSet

namespace DelaunayStretch

/-- **Lemma 4.2 (Range of the coordinates)** (p.22).

1. The angular coordinates of every gate state lie in `Σ`. Conversely, for every `z ∈ Σ`,
   there is a gate state with angular coordinates `z`, and it is unique up to translations along
   the `x`-axis and scalings with positive ratio centered at points of the `x`-axis.
2. Let `s = (O, G, δ)` be a gate state, where `O` has center `o` and radius `r`, with angular
   coordinates `(γ, φ, θ, ψ)`. Then the upper and the lower arc of `O` have lengths `r(π + 2γ)`
   and `r(π − 2γ)`; the part of the upper arc from `w₋(O)` to `aG` has length `r(θ + γ − φ)`,
   and the part of the lower arc from `w₋(O)` to `bG` has length `r(θ − γ + φ)`, so that the
   arc of `∂O` from `aG` to `bG` through `w₋(O)` has central angle `2θ`;
   `x(w±(O)) = x(o) ± r cos γ`; and `x(c(s)) − x(o) = r (sin γ sin φ − cos θ)/cos φ` (4.1).

Mo, Cheng, Ding, *The Stretch Factor of Planar Delaunay Triangulations Is Nearly Determined*,
preprint (arXiv:2609.07979, version not stamped; held file of November 3, 2026), Lemma 4.2, p.22.

**Formalization Note** "Unique up to …" is: two gate states with the same angular coordinates
are images of each other under `p ↦ k p + t` (`k > 0`, `t ∈ ℝ`), applied to the center, the
gate ends, the radius and `δ` (`GateState.scaleTranslate`); these maps are exactly the
compositions of translations along the `x`-axis and scalings with positive ratio centered at
points of the `x`-axis. The central angle `2θ` of the arc from `aG` to `bG` through `w₋(O)`
is stated as: the sum of the two arc lengths from `w₋(O)` is `r · 2θ`. -/
theorem lemma_4_2_range_of_coordinates :
    (∀ s : GateState, s.IsGateState → s.angularCoords ∈ SigmaSet) ∧
    (∀ z ∈ SigmaSet, ∃ s : GateState, s.IsGateState ∧ s.angularCoords = z) ∧
    (∀ s s' : GateState, s.IsGateState → s'.IsGateState → s.angularCoords = s'.angularCoords →
      ∃ k t : ℝ, 0 < k ∧ s' = s.scaleTranslate k t) ∧
    (∀ s : GateState, s.IsGateState →
      s.O.upperArcLength s.O.wMinus s.O.wPlus = s.O.radius * (Real.pi + 2 * s.gammaCoord) ∧
      s.O.lowerArcLength s.O.wMinus s.O.wPlus = s.O.radius * (Real.pi - 2 * s.gammaCoord) ∧
      s.O.upperArcLength s.O.wMinus s.aG =
        s.O.radius * (s.thetaCoord + s.gammaCoord - s.phiCoord) ∧
      s.O.lowerArcLength s.O.wMinus s.bG =
        s.O.radius * (s.thetaCoord - s.gammaCoord + s.phiCoord) ∧
      s.O.upperArcLength s.O.wMinus s.aG + s.O.lowerArcLength s.O.wMinus s.bG =
        s.O.radius * (2 * s.thetaCoord) ∧
      s.O.wMinus.re = s.O.center.re - s.O.radius * Real.cos s.gammaCoord ∧
      s.O.wPlus.re = s.O.center.re + s.O.radius * Real.cos s.gammaCoord ∧
      s.crossing.re - s.O.center.re =
        s.O.radius * (Real.sin s.gammaCoord * Real.sin s.phiCoord - Real.cos s.thetaCoord) /
          Real.cos s.phiCoord) := by sorry

end DelaunayStretch
